# LlamaIndex RAG Best Practices

## Overview

LlamaIndex (formerly GPT Index) is a data framework for building Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) applications. It provides tools to ingest, structure, and access private or domain-specific data for use with Large Language Models (LLMs), enabling context-aware AI applications that can reason over your own data.

## Core Principles

- Use LlamaIndex for building sophisticated RAG applications with document indexing and retrieval
- Implement proper document loading and preprocessing with appropriate text splitters
- Configure vector stores and embedding models for optimal semantic search performance
- Use appropriate index types (VectorStoreIndex, TreeIndex, ListIndex) based on use case requirements
- Implement query engines with proper retrieval and response synthesis strategies
- Use prompt templates and response synthesizers for consistent and relevant outputs
- Configure metadata filtering and semantic search for enhanced retrieval precision
- Implement proper evaluation metrics for RAG system performance assessment
- Use LlamaIndex's agent framework for complex multi-step reasoning and tool use
- Monitor retrieval quality and implement optimization strategies for production systems

